  "notes": "Per setting: non-FSM genuine-vs-false metrics per method. allSJ3 = keep an isoform iff every junction has >= 3 unique short reads (SQANTI3 min_cov). SQ3strict = SQANTI3 rules filter with min_cov >= 3 required. SQ3ml uses SQANTI3's default TP/TN (FSM vs NNC) which is mismatched to this simulation (most NNC are genuine), so it is reported but not used for conclusions. Conclusion: PanIsoGuard is not more accurate than a one-line short-read rule; PIG+bam's small AUPRC gain is within the bootstrap CI at every depth since 0.0.6 (the BAM gate needs >= 3 spanning reads). With no short reads and no BAM it confirms nothing; with the BAM it ranks above SQANTI3's default rules and level with the caller's own read count (read_count_baseline: the caller's count as a filter and a ranking, SQANTI3's rules with FL >= k required, the whole-chain read count alone; count_baseline.py).",
